1
00:00:01,584 --> 00:00:02,711
<i>Attorney.</i>

2
00:00:03,628 --> 00:00:06,589
<i>I can request to speak to Billy, right?</i>

3
00:00:08,174 --> 00:00:11,177
<i>I can just relay your message to her.</i>

4
00:00:12,303 --> 00:00:13,179
<i>No.</i>

5
00:00:13,263 --> 00:00:17,142
<i>I have to tell her myself.</i>
<i>We need to talk in person.</i>

6
00:00:21,521 --> 00:00:22,731
<i>Enrico.</i>

7
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:26,651
<i>Enrico, you're starting to worry me.</i>
<i>Is your blood sugar still low?</i>

8
00:00:27,318 --> 00:00:28,278
<i>Wait right here.</i>

9
00:00:28,361 --> 00:00:29,821
<i>Precious.</i>

10
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:35,660
<i>I have something</i>

11
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:37,829
<i>to tell you and Billy.</i>

12
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:40,081
<i>Hello, Attorney?</i>

13
00:00:40,165 --> 00:00:43,334
<i>I just got off the phone</i>
<i>with Atty. Reyes, Bea's lawyer.</i>

14
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:45,712
<i>Bea asked to speak with you in person.</i>

15
00:00:46,296 --> 00:00:47,797
<i>Why?</i>

16
00:00:47,881 --> 00:00:49,257
<i>She wouldn't say.</i>

17
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:53,344
<i>Can't she just say whatever it is</i>
<i>through her lawyer?</i>

18
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:55,597
[SIGHS] <i>Bea's adamant.</i>

19
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:58,224
<i>She insists it's a… family matter?</i>

20
00:00:59,350 --> 00:01:00,351
<i>Okay.</i>

21
00:01:01,144 --> 00:01:03,646
<i>I'll pay her a visit. Thank you.</i>

22
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:05,690
HOUSE RAZED BY FIRE
ELDEST DAUGHTER DEAD, MOTHER HURT

23
00:01:05,774 --> 00:01:07,692
[ENRICO]<i> I want to apologize to them too.</i>

24
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:13,948
<i>They're your family?</i>

25
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:18,244
<i>Bea Mercado is your daughter?</i>

26
00:01:18,953 --> 00:01:21,706
<i>Are you married to Mariela Mercado?</i>

27
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:23,875
<i>How do you know them?</i>

28
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:27,754
<i>Enrico, it wasn't an accident</i>
<i>when our house caught fire.</i>

29
00:01:28,713 --> 00:01:30,590
<i>It was Mariela's doing.</i>

30
00:01:32,133 --> 00:01:33,593
<i>How is that possible?</i>

31
00:01:33,676 --> 00:01:35,553
<i>They're in jail.</i>

32
00:01:36,679 --> 00:01:39,057
<i>Both Mariela and Bea, your daughter.</i>

33
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:41,893
<i>She hid her mother from the police.</i>

34
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:44,979
<i>But that's not at all, Enrico.</i>
<i>There's more.</i>

35
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:48,483
<i>Billy has filed many more cases</i>
<i>against them.</i>

36
00:01:48,566 --> 00:01:50,819
<i>They wouldn't leave her alone.</i>

37
00:01:50,902 --> 00:01:52,987
<i>They wanted to ruin her life.</i>

38
00:01:53,071 --> 00:01:54,823
<i>Jordan! Oh my God!</i>

39
00:01:54,906 --> 00:01:56,866
<i>Our video went viral!</i>

40
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:59,744
<i>Three hundred thousand views!</i>
<i>Look, look, look! Look!</i>

41
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:02,455
<i>That's great.</i>
<i>But, Val, that can wait.</i>

42
00:02:02,539 --> 00:02:04,124
<i>Huh? Why?</i>

43
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:08,294
[VALERIE GASPS]

44
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:09,879
<i>Oh my God.</i>

45
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:12,423
<i>Oh my gosh, Billy, I'm so sorry.</i>

46
00:02:12,507 --> 00:02:13,633
[BILLY] <i>It's fine.</i>

47
00:02:13,716 --> 00:02:19,556
<i>I just got so excited because</i>
<i>I uploaded a video of him singing, and…</i>

48
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:21,766
<i>I don't know.</i>

49
00:02:21,850 --> 00:02:24,227
<i>That evening, when he was singing,</i>

50
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:26,062
<i>there was just something in him.</i>

51
00:02:26,146 --> 00:02:28,189
<i>With the way he sang the song.</i>

52
00:02:28,273 --> 00:02:30,108
<i>How do I put this? Um…</i>

53
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:32,819
<i>Heartfelt? Special?</i>

54
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:37,907
["PAUWI NA" PLAYING OVER PHONE]

55
00:02:37,991 --> 00:02:41,202
[VALERIE]<i> And your performance</i>
<i>was super sincere.</i>

56
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:42,370
<i>It was like…</i>

57
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:45,957
<i>You could really feel that</i>
<i>you were in love--</i>

58
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,000
[JORDAN] <i>Val.</i>

59
00:02:47,083 --> 00:02:49,002
<i>Why? I'm just stating facts.</i>

60
00:02:49,919 --> 00:02:53,172
<i>As you sang, it was like</i>
<i>you poured everything out.</i>

61
00:02:54,299 --> 00:02:57,594
<i>Everyone felt it because you were</i>
<i>being honest, Jordan.</i>

62
00:02:58,261 --> 00:03:01,389
<i>Except for that one person</i>
<i>you dedicated that song to.</i>

63
00:03:02,765 --> 00:03:04,100
<i>The person you love.</i>

64
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:07,645
["PAUWI NA" KEEPS PLAYING]

65
00:03:11,482 --> 00:03:12,692
[MUSIC FADES]

66
00:03:21,159 --> 00:03:22,952
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

67
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:24,412
You wanted to speak with me.

68
00:03:26,247 --> 00:03:29,042
I don't have all day.
I'm a busy person.

69
00:03:31,085 --> 00:03:32,587
Billy, sorry.

70
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:37,050
Have you run out of tricks
to escape from this?

71
00:03:37,133 --> 00:03:41,304
Your apology won't erase
all the harm you've done to my family.

72
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:44,515
I trusted you, Bea. Remember?

73
00:03:45,266 --> 00:03:46,935
I tried to understand you.

74
00:03:47,018 --> 00:03:49,854
I asked you countless times
for your motive,

75
00:03:49,938 --> 00:03:51,564
but I never got an answer.

76
00:03:52,398 --> 00:03:55,610
You just kept making things worse
for my family.

77
00:03:56,402 --> 00:03:57,403
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

78
00:03:57,487 --> 00:04:01,199
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

79
00:04:01,282 --> 00:04:02,617
Billy, you're right.

80
00:04:03,534 --> 00:04:05,161
I wronged you.

81
00:04:05,245 --> 00:04:07,372
I wronged your family too.

82
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:12,710
I did it because you stole from me.

83
00:04:12,794 --> 00:04:15,129
Bullshit! I never stole anything from you.

84
00:04:15,213 --> 00:04:17,590
You tore my family apart, Billy.

85
00:04:17,674 --> 00:04:20,343
Because you stole my father from us.

86
00:04:20,969 --> 00:04:26,182
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

87
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:27,600
[MUSIC FADES]

88
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:34,649
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

89
00:04:37,944 --> 00:04:39,821
Are you really that desperate?

90
00:04:39,904 --> 00:04:41,197
Billy, it's the truth.

91
00:04:41,281 --> 00:04:43,366
And do you think I'll believe you?

92
00:04:43,449 --> 00:04:46,286
And then what? I'll drop the charges
against you and your mother?

93
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:47,370
Billy?

94
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:53,167
[MUSIC SWELLING]

95
00:04:53,251 --> 00:04:55,336
[MUSIC FADING]

96
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:56,921
Bea?

97
00:04:57,005 --> 00:04:58,089
Sweetheart?

98
00:04:59,215 --> 00:05:04,929
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

99
00:05:12,061 --> 00:05:18,776
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

100
00:05:56,022 --> 00:06:00,526
[HEAVY SILENCE]

101
00:06:06,616 --> 00:06:08,576
Just when did you plan on telling me?

102
00:06:08,659 --> 00:06:12,663
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

103
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:14,207
A long time ago.

104
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,294
I just didn't know how.

105
00:06:19,212 --> 00:06:20,671
I was afraid that

106
00:06:21,255 --> 00:06:23,007
I might hurt you again.

107
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:26,427
I tried to find you both,

108
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:30,556
so I could make up for leaving
all those years ago.

109
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:32,558
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

110
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:34,435
But then I found you first.

111
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:38,898
When you left us…

112
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:44,112
I knew you probably had another family.

113
00:06:46,906 --> 00:06:49,534
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

114
00:06:49,617 --> 00:06:51,494
But why her?

115
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:03,005
[BILLY BREATHES DEEPLY]

116
00:07:04,715 --> 00:07:07,009
I'm asking again for forgiveness, dear.

117
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:10,847
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

118
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:12,306
From both of you.

119
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:17,979
Forgiveness?

120
00:07:19,981 --> 00:07:21,274
Are you serious?

121
00:07:22,108 --> 00:07:24,694
You're seriously asking for forgiveness?

122
00:07:24,777 --> 00:07:26,612
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

123
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:27,780
Now?

124
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:29,699
[SCOFFS]

125
00:07:30,783 --> 00:07:33,453
Are you even aware
of everything that happened?

126
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:37,290
When my mother found out

127
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:41,252
you had another woman, a mistress,

128
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:43,546
do you know what she did?

129
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:45,131
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

130
00:07:45,214 --> 00:07:47,550
She tried to kill herself.

131
00:07:48,176 --> 00:07:50,428
And one more thing you might not know.

132
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:51,846
We lost our home in a fire,

133
00:07:51,929 --> 00:07:53,890
and my sister died.

134
00:07:53,973 --> 00:07:55,600
It was all because of you.

135
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:57,935
All of it was because of you!

136
00:07:59,187 --> 00:08:02,482
Our lives wouldn't have been destroyed

137
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:08,613
if only you had been
a responsible father and husband.

138
00:08:08,696 --> 00:08:10,114
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

139
00:08:10,198 --> 00:08:14,076
Sure, my mother isn't perfect.

140
00:08:15,536 --> 00:08:18,289
She's not perfect, but she loved you.

141
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:20,833
With all her heart.

142
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:26,422
My sister and I loved you too.

143
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:28,090
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

144
00:08:28,174 --> 00:08:29,467
But what did you do?

145
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:32,512
What did you do?!

146
00:08:33,971 --> 00:08:35,640
You replaced us.

147
00:08:37,058 --> 00:08:38,601
You abandoned us!

148
00:08:41,395 --> 00:08:42,855
[HUFFS]

149
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:45,066
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

150
00:08:45,149 --> 00:08:46,984
Honestly, I don't get it.

151
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:52,156
I don't why I was even hopeful.

152
00:08:52,657 --> 00:08:53,658
You know?

153
00:08:55,618 --> 00:08:57,537
I hoped…

154
00:08:59,872 --> 00:09:01,874
when our house burned down,

155
00:09:02,917 --> 00:09:05,711
when my mother lost her sanity,
when my sister died--

156
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:08,214
I don't know why
I expected you to come back.

157
00:09:09,131 --> 00:09:10,424
I hoped you would.

158
00:09:10,508 --> 00:09:11,717
[BEA SNIFFLES]

159
00:09:11,801 --> 00:09:14,136
My sister died.
Your daughter died!

160
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:17,807
She was your daughter!
Your eldest daughter!

161
00:09:18,432 --> 00:09:19,767
But you never returned.

162
00:09:19,850 --> 00:09:24,021
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

163
00:09:24,689 --> 00:09:26,399
What, that's it?

164
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:29,151
You just disappeared?

165
00:09:30,319 --> 00:09:34,031
If you couldn't treat us as your family,

166
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:36,993
you could've at least treated us
as human beings!

167
00:09:38,286 --> 00:09:40,580
We were asking for so little!

168
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:44,709
At least shown a little concern,
a little compassion!

169
00:09:44,792 --> 00:09:46,711
Even just a little pity!

170
00:09:46,794 --> 00:09:48,296
Do you understand? Just a little pity!

171
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:49,672
But no!

172
00:09:50,548 --> 00:09:53,301
You left me all alone, Papa!

173
00:09:53,384 --> 00:09:54,844
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

174
00:09:54,927 --> 00:09:55,928
[BANGS TABLE]

175
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:58,306
[CRIES] You left me, Papa!

176
00:09:58,389 --> 00:09:59,515
[ENRICO BREATHES SHAKILY]

177
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:01,350
[ENRICO] I'm here now, sweetheart.

178
00:10:01,434 --> 00:10:02,476
[SIGHS]

179
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:05,062
I'll make it up to you.

180
00:10:05,146 --> 00:10:06,397
Too late!

181
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:08,441
Sure, you're back! But it's too late!

182
00:10:08,524 --> 00:10:09,984
You can't change anything now!

183
00:10:10,067 --> 00:10:12,236
- Nothing at all!
- [GROANS]

184
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,696
Dad?

185
00:10:14,363 --> 00:10:15,281
Dad!

186
00:10:15,364 --> 00:10:17,158
[RAGGED BREATHS]

187
00:10:17,241 --> 00:10:18,326
Papa?

188
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:19,994
What--

189
00:10:20,077 --> 00:10:24,206
[LABORED BREATHS]

190
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:25,291
Sir!

191
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:28,252
- Help!
- Sir, we need help!

192
00:10:28,336 --> 00:10:29,420
[BEA] Help!

193
00:10:29,503 --> 00:10:32,006
- [MUSIC FADING]
- [TRAFFIC NOISE IN DISTANCE]

194
00:10:32,590 --> 00:10:35,051
Enrico has entered
the advanced stage of heart failure,

195
00:10:35,134 --> 00:10:37,637
and this has been developing
for quite some time.

196
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:39,472
His arteries are blocked,

197
00:10:39,555 --> 00:10:42,141
leading to ischemic heart disease.

198
00:10:42,224 --> 00:10:46,812
His condition has been
further worsened by his diabetes.

199
00:10:46,896 --> 00:10:51,651
- [MACHINE BEEPING STEADILY]
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

200
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:53,444
Why didn't you tell us?

201
00:10:54,570 --> 00:10:56,822
I didn't tell you because

202
00:10:57,698 --> 00:11:01,786
I didn't want you to think
that was the reason

203
00:11:01,869 --> 00:11:03,704
I'm asking for your forgiveness.

204
00:11:03,788 --> 00:11:08,542
I just want to spend my remaining days…

205
00:11:08,626 --> 00:11:12,463
[MACHINE BEEPING STEADILY]

206
00:11:12,546 --> 00:11:14,215
…with you.

207
00:11:15,466 --> 00:11:19,762
I want us to patch things up
and be a family.

208
00:11:19,845 --> 00:11:22,515
That is all I want.

209
00:11:23,307 --> 00:11:24,892
I'm sorry, my dear.

210
00:11:24,975 --> 00:11:30,898
- [MACHINE BEEPING STEADILY]
- [SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

211
00:11:30,981 --> 00:11:33,651
What procedure can you do for my father?

212
00:11:33,734 --> 00:11:40,741
[MUSIC TURNS HOPEFUL]

213
00:11:45,413 --> 00:11:46,372
Bea?

214
00:11:47,081 --> 00:11:48,749
What did your father say?

215
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:56,340
[INHALES] Um…

216
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:00,970
He apologized, Ma.

217
00:12:05,182 --> 00:12:06,934
He wants to make things right.

218
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:10,563
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

219
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:12,773
But I told him everything.

220
00:12:16,777 --> 00:12:18,779
All the anger

221
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:26,245
and all the pain he caused us.

222
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:31,208
[INHALES]

223
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:32,877
Then…

224
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:40,301
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

225
00:12:40,384 --> 00:12:42,636
He suddenly collapsed.

226
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:43,679
What?

227
00:12:44,263 --> 00:12:45,806
I think…

228
00:12:46,891 --> 00:12:48,684
I think he had a heart attack.

229
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:56,192
[MUSIC TURNS MOROSE]

230
00:12:57,735 --> 00:12:59,361
[MARIELA SOBS SOFTLY]

231
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:05,743
Ma?

232
00:13:07,953 --> 00:13:09,747
Are you worried about him?

233
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:12,166
Seriously?

234
00:13:14,335 --> 00:13:16,337
I thought you wanted him dead?

235
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:23,260
You said he apologized
and wants to make things right.

236
00:13:23,344 --> 00:13:26,847
Maybe he could get us out of here then.

237
00:13:29,808 --> 00:13:36,774
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

238
00:13:38,442 --> 00:13:39,610
Yes, Ma.

239
00:13:41,278 --> 00:13:42,488
You're right.

240
00:13:44,281 --> 00:13:47,034
That was always the plan.

241
00:13:48,702 --> 00:13:49,703
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

242
00:13:49,787 --> 00:13:53,123
If we exploit their kindness,

243
00:13:53,207 --> 00:13:55,209
we can get out of here.

244
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:57,044
Then…

245
00:14:00,047 --> 00:14:01,715
we're going to destroy them again.

246
00:14:01,799 --> 00:14:05,844
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

247
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:08,973
We're going to destroy their family.

248
00:14:09,056 --> 00:14:11,850
Then we'll get your father back.

249
00:14:13,310 --> 00:14:14,520
After that,

250
00:14:15,771 --> 00:14:17,648
our family will be together again.

251
00:14:17,731 --> 00:14:24,196
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

252
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:27,491
If we can get your father to side with us,

253
00:14:28,826 --> 00:14:30,870
we can definitely get out of here.

254
00:14:31,787 --> 00:14:34,081
Even if Billy is against it.

255
00:14:34,164 --> 00:14:37,877
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

256
00:14:40,212 --> 00:14:41,297
Listen, Bea.

257
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:46,510
I need you to do something.

258
00:14:47,469 --> 00:14:52,516
Find out how your father's doing.

259
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:58,063
[DARK MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

260
00:15:06,322 --> 00:15:08,407
[MACHINE BEEPING STEADILY]

261
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:11,452
[DOCTOR] <i>Because he has</i>
<i>a weak heart and diabetes,</i>

262
00:15:11,535 --> 00:15:13,621
<i>an open-heart surgery is too risky.</i>

263
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:19,752
<i>That's why I'm recommending</i>
<i>a procedure called MitraClip.</i>

264
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:22,796
<i>Instead of opening his chest,</i>

265
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:25,466
<i>we're going to perform</i>
<i>a percutaneous repair.</i>

266
00:15:26,675 --> 00:15:31,305
<i>But given his condition,</i>
<i>we need to be prepared for anything.</i>

267
00:15:31,388 --> 00:15:36,185
[HOPEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

268
00:15:40,439 --> 00:15:41,398
Billy?

269
00:15:42,524 --> 00:15:45,277
Oliver is with your Auntie Lydia.

270
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:52,368
Thank God your father is out of danger.

271
00:15:53,035 --> 00:15:54,662
His surgery was a success.

272
00:15:57,831 --> 00:16:01,210
I thought this was a fresh start for us.

273
00:16:02,127 --> 00:16:06,924
I thought Oliver
would finally have a father.

274
00:16:07,007 --> 00:16:08,926
But why did he do this, Auntie Pres?

275
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:11,512
He lied again.

276
00:16:11,595 --> 00:16:13,764
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

277
00:16:13,847 --> 00:16:16,392
We don't know his reason.

278
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:19,228
But even with all
these unanswered questions,

279
00:16:19,311 --> 00:16:21,522
you are still here.

280
00:16:21,605 --> 00:16:22,982
By his side.

281
00:16:24,274 --> 00:16:26,485
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

282
00:16:26,568 --> 00:16:28,445
I admire your compassion.

283
00:16:29,029 --> 00:16:31,782
Despite how you feel about your father,

284
00:16:31,865 --> 00:16:33,409
about Bea,

285
00:16:33,492 --> 00:16:36,286
you still gave him
the treatment he needed.

286
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:39,581
Because of you,

287
00:16:40,541 --> 00:16:44,044
he has a chance to make things right.

288
00:16:44,628 --> 00:16:51,093
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

289
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:04,481
Here, Grandpa.

290
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:06,567
Be careful.

291
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:15,159
Grandpa.

292
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:17,453
Look at this.

293
00:17:19,413 --> 00:17:22,082
[JORDAN SINGING IN VIDEO]
<i>♪ My muse ♪</i>

294
00:17:22,166 --> 00:17:24,043
Almost half a million views.

295
00:17:24,126 --> 00:17:28,005
<i>♪ Where's our destination? ♪</i>

296
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:31,091
<i>♪ You are the captain ♪</i>

297
00:17:31,175 --> 00:17:35,262
<i>♪ I'll follow wherever you go ♪</i>

298
00:17:35,345 --> 00:17:36,930
<i>♪ Oh, baby… ♪</i>

299
00:17:37,014 --> 00:17:38,766
That's my daughter's song.

300
00:17:38,849 --> 00:17:39,933
Jade wrote that!

301
00:17:40,017 --> 00:17:41,560
That's right, Grandpa!

302
00:17:41,643 --> 00:17:44,021
- Yes.
- [JUDE CHUCKLES]

303
00:17:44,104 --> 00:17:46,732
I just tweaked the lyrics a bit.

304
00:17:46,815 --> 00:17:48,192
[SINGING CONTINUES ON VIDEO]

305
00:17:48,275 --> 00:17:52,571
That song is for
the two women I love the most.

306
00:17:54,031 --> 00:17:55,032
Yeah…

307
00:17:55,115 --> 00:18:02,122
My daughter wrote this song for her son

308
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:04,500
and her husband.

309
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:08,337
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you</i>
<i>Everything changed? ♪</i>

310
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,296
[VIDEO STOPS]

311
00:18:09,379 --> 00:18:16,261
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

312
00:18:35,739 --> 00:18:37,658
- Can I help you?
- [DRIVER] We're the caterers.

313
00:18:37,741 --> 00:18:38,867
Straight ahead.

314
00:18:40,702 --> 00:18:42,121
[ENGINE REVS]

315
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:55,134
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

316
00:19:11,733 --> 00:19:18,740
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

317
00:19:20,868 --> 00:19:22,327
[INMATE SHOUTS]

318
00:19:25,455 --> 00:19:31,378
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

319
00:19:36,091 --> 00:19:38,510
- Is the food ready?
- Yes.

320
00:19:41,346 --> 00:19:42,931
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

321
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:44,183
- [THUDS]
- Watch it, man.

322
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:45,976
- [SHRILL WHISTLE]
- [OBJECTS CLATTER]

323
00:19:46,059 --> 00:19:47,853
- Hey!
- You bastard!

324
00:19:47,936 --> 00:19:49,229
- [GRUNTS]
- [BLOW LANDS]

325
00:19:49,313 --> 00:19:50,189
[CLAMORING]

326
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:52,399
- Give me your clothes. Go!
- [GUARD WHISTLING]

327
00:19:53,025 --> 00:19:54,610
- [BLOWS LAND]
- [INMATES CLAMORING]

328
00:19:54,693 --> 00:19:56,111
[GUARD WHISTLING]

329
00:19:56,195 --> 00:19:58,655
[CLAMORING]

330
00:19:58,739 --> 00:20:00,282
- Get down! Down!
- [THWACKS]

331
00:20:00,365 --> 00:20:01,992
[GUARD WHISTLING]

332
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:10,542
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

333
00:20:10,626 --> 00:20:11,543
Hurry up!

334
00:20:11,627 --> 00:20:18,592
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

335
00:20:31,396 --> 00:20:33,565
<i>I know that</i>
<i>your hospital bills are piling up.</i>

336
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:35,943
<i>Please, let me help.</i>

337
00:20:36,026 --> 00:20:38,111
<i>Of course we got</i>
<i>each other's backs.</i>

338
00:20:38,946 --> 00:20:41,490
<i>- Where are Ms. Mariela and Bea?</i>
<i>- Why?! Who are you?!</i>

339
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:43,533
<i>Answer my question,</i>
<i>or I'll smash your face with this.</i>

340
00:20:43,617 --> 00:20:46,870
[MARIELA] <i>Any update</i>
<i>on your father?</i>

341
00:20:46,954 --> 00:20:49,206
<i>- Nothing yet, Ma.</i>
<i>- What if he died?</i>

342
00:20:49,831 --> 00:20:52,209
<i>Or worse, what if he's still alive</i>

343
00:20:52,292 --> 00:20:55,462
<i>but his bastard child</i>
<i>brainwashed him</i>

344
00:20:55,545 --> 00:20:57,256
<i>into forgetting about us?</i>

345
00:21:00,217 --> 00:21:04,638
<i>I don't know if she's sincerely</i>
<i>asking for forgiveness.</i>

346
00:21:04,721 --> 00:21:08,058
<i>She might be planning something</i>
<i>against us again.</i>

347
00:21:08,141 --> 00:21:11,186
<i>The company is literally</i>
<i>bleeding right now.</i>

348
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:13,981
<i>Let's hear some solutions.</i>

349
00:21:14,064 --> 00:21:15,524
<i>A solution that actually works.</i>

350
00:21:15,607 --> 00:21:16,984
<i>Let's regroup tomorrow morning.</i>

351
00:21:17,067 --> 00:21:18,360
<i>Tomorrow is Saturday.</i>

352
00:21:18,443 --> 00:21:19,778
<i>Dude, sorry.</i>

353
00:21:19,861 --> 00:21:21,571
<i>Maybe we can do</i>
<i>a Zoom meeting?</i>

354
00:21:21,655 --> 00:21:22,906
<i>It's fine.</i>

355
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:24,908
<i>- Sunday?</i>
<i>- No. I'll see you Monday.</i>

356
00:21:24,992 --> 00:21:25,867
<i>Billy?</i>

357
00:21:25,951 --> 00:21:28,120
<i>Where's your commitment</i>
<i>to your work?</i>
